{
  "name": "The Sandpits",
  "finish": {
    "x": 5510,
    "y": 452
  },
  "description": "Seven apples and six sand pits along a dry wash in the late afternoon. Every pit has a floor, and each asks something different. Pit 1 (150 wide) is the meeting: a low kicker clears it at any speed, with the apple floating over it. The kicker pit: ride down into it. Its apple floats at lip height, and only the kicker on its floor throws you up to it. The turn pit: its west rim is a kicker facing back the way you came, with the apple high over the lip, out of reach going east. Ride down and up the long east ramp, let the bike roll back, turn and drive west off the kicker, land on the slope behind it, then turn again and ride on. The twin pits ask for measured speed: at full gas you overshoot the short table between them onto the second kicker. Ease off and land on the table. The big pit under the sandstone arch is the opposite: full gas off the tallest kicker, and level the bike for the apple under the arch and the far lip, 270 units away. Then the terraces: a shelf, and a steep face into the dig. The apple waits at the foot of the face: roll down it slowly, leaning back, or you fly over it. Last, the dig: carry what speed you can across its floor and up the long climb to the mesa, where the flower floats over the crest. Intended apple order 1 to 7. Every miss lands on a floor with a way out; only a crash ends the run.",
